From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] setupapi, cfgmgr32: logical configurations and hardware profiles

CM_Get_First_Log_Conf(_Ex) check the device and flags and report CR_NO_MORE_LOG_CONF -- no device here has a resource list, since no driver assigns hardware resources -- so CM_Get_Next_Log_Conf, CM_Get_Log_Conf_Priority and CM_Free_Log_Conf_Handle see no valid handle. CM_Get_Hardware_Profile_Info(_Ex)A/W report the one, current hardware profile (IDConfigDB CurrentConfig, 0001 by default; its stored friendly name or "Profile N"), not dockable; CM_Get_HW_Prof_Flags(_Ex)A/W read a device's CSConfigFlags from the profile's Enum copy, none by default. They were spec stubs (device tools crashed on them); cfgmgr32 forwards them; cfgmgr32.h gains the types and prototypes.
---
--- a/include/cfgmgr32.h
+++ b/include/cfgmgr32.h
